\section{Enrichment Providers}
\label{sec:enrichment-providers}

Not all providers support DOI lookups or provide abstracts.
We define which providers to use for enrichment and in what order.

Unlike search (where we query multiple providers and merge the resulting paper
sets), enrichment starts from an existing paper record and fills in missing
fields.
To maximize coverage, we try multiple providers in sequence and keep going as
long as any requested fields are still missing.

We also skip providers that are not configured. For example, IEEE Xplore and Web
of Science require API keys; if they are not available, we move on to the next
provider.

\begin{description}
\item[Semantic Scholar] Excellent abstract coverage, free API with optional
  key for higher rate limits.
\item[arXiv] When a paper is an arXiv preprint, arXiv provides the abstract.
\item[OpenAlex] Very broad coverage (250M+ works), always free.
\item[IEEE Xplore] Strong coverage for IEEE publications.
  Requires an API key.
\item[Web of Science] High-quality bibliographic metadata.
  Requires an API key.
\end{description}

<<constants>>=
# Providers to try for DOI-based metadata enrichment (in priority order)
ENRICHMENT_PROVIDERS = ["s2", "arxiv", "openalex", "ieee", "wos"]

# Global cache for enriched paper data (refs/cites)
# Stored in data dir (not cache dir) since fetching refs/cites is expensive
ENRICHMENT_CACHE_DIR = "enrichment_cache"
